hrough sorted features to assign individuals to subpopulations. Key variables include \\\( sf_k \\\), \\\( SortedFeature \\\), and \\\( SortedIndividual \\\).\r\n␀)/K 5/P 20967 0 R/Pg 240 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj20999 0 obj<</K 6/P 20967 0 R/Pg 240 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj21000 0 obj<</K 8/P 20967 0 R/Pg 240 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj21001 0 obj<</K 10/P 20967 0 R/Pg 240 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj21002 0 obj<</K[1 21395 0 R 3]/P 20967 0 R/Pg 244 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj21003 0 obj<</A 21394 0 R/Alt(The image is a pseudocode algorithm for updating an archive in a population-based optimization process. It includes inputs: \\\( A \\\) \(the archive\), \\\( O \\\) \(the new population\), and \\\( N \\\) \(the population size\). The outputs are \\\( A' \\\\) \(the updated archive\) and \\\( g_{\\text{best}} \\\) \(the updated global optima\). The steps involve merging archives, ranking individuals based on classification error and selected features, calculating fitness, sorting, and preserving top individu\als. Mathematical symbols include \\\( A' \\\), \\\( R_i^1 \\\), and \\\( R_i^2 \\\).\r\n␀)/K 4/P 20967 0 R/Pg 244 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj21004 0 obj<</K 5/P 20967 0 R/Pg 244 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj21005 0 obj<</K 7/P 20967 0 R/Pg 244 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj21006 0 obj<</K[9 21388 0 R 11 21389 0 R 13 21390 0 R 15]/P 20967 0 R/Pg 244 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj21007 0 obj<</K 18/P 20967 0 R/Pg 244 0 R/S/H2/Type/StructElem>>endobj21008 0 obj<</K 20/P 20967 0 R/Pg 244 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj21009 0 obj<</A 21387 0 R/Alt(Algorithm flowchart for feature selection using a genetic algorithm. The process begins with initializing a population and applying a feature niching technique. It iterates through generations, performing mutation and crossover operations to find optimal \solutions. The algorithm ranks and selects feature subsets, storing them in an archive. K